    "abstract": "An article or method of heat exchange, comprise a component 1    with two or more portions 2    - 6â   each with selected amounts of La, Fe, Si and one or more elements T and R suitable to produce a La1-aRa(Fe1-x-yTySix)13Hz phase, wherein T is one or more of the elements from Mn, Co, Ni and Cr and R is one or more of the elements Ce, Nd, Y and Pr. The selected amounts of at least one of T, R and a selected amount of Si are chosen to provide the respective portions 2   - 6    with different Curie temperatures Tc. The said selected amounts may further provide similar sinter activities for the said potions and a monolithic component 1    may be provided via a single sinter process. The two or more sintered portions 2    - 6    may each have a different Curie temperature and a density within a range of Â± 5% or Â± 2% of an average density of all the sintered portions. The article and method provides a monolithic magnetic heat exchanger which may operate over a broader temperature range and can be more readily worked into a suitable shape with a reduced risk of cracking.",
